{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Mandate 25% urban tree canopy targets to protect public health and the NHS",
        "additional_details": "Extreme heatwaves can place severe strain on the heart, causing spikes in cardiac arrests that put an unsustainable burden on an already stretched NHS. Surfaces like tarmac can turn housing into heat traps, leaving homebuyers vulnerable to unliveable conditions.\r\n\r\nTrees provide vital cooling, dropping local surface temperatures by up to 15\u00b0C through shade and evapotranspiration. We ask Parliament to mandate 25% tree canopy targets, reducing NHS costs and relieving communities of unbearable heat.",
        "background": "Legislate to require a minimum 25% urban tree canopy cover target in the Environment Act and in the National Planning Policy Framework for all new developments and require existing urban areas to reach at least 25% tree canopy cover by 2050.",
